# Bloodline Architecture Rules

## Core Architecture

- Use App Router only.
- Never use Pages Router.
- Never use getServerSideProps or getStaticProps.
- Use Server Components by default.
- Add `"use client"` only when browser interaction is required.
- Prefer ISR and static rendering whenever possible.

---

## Folder Rules

- `src/app` is for routes only.
- `src/components` is for reusable UI and sections only.
- `src/config` contains all regional business truth.
- `src/content` contains MDX content only.
- `src/lib` contains reusable business logic and utilities.
- `src/data` contains cached/generated datasets.
- `src/types` contains shared TypeScript types.

Do not place business logic inside components unnecessarily.

---

## Regional Content Rules

- Never hardcode regional business content inside components.
- All region-specific data must come from `src/config/regions`.
- Components must receive regional content through props or helpers.
- Domain detection must remain centralized.

Forbidden example:

```tsx
<h1>Best Tattoo Studio in Bangkok</h1>
```

Preferred:

```tsx
<h1>{region.hero.heading}</h1>
```

---

## Rendering Rules

- Prefer Server Components.
- Keep Client Components isolated and small.
- Do not make entire pages client-rendered unnecessarily.
- SEO-critical content must remain server-rendered.
- Avoid unnecessary hydration.

---

## Data Rules

- Use config for stable business truth.
- Use MDX for long-form SEO content.
- Use Airtable only for operational/media content.
- Use cached JSON for reviews.
- Never fetch Airtable directly inside UI components.
- Centralize external fetchers inside `src/lib`.

---

## Route Rules

- Follow the locked route blueprint.
- Use kebab-case URLs only.
- Do not invent new route categories.
- No artist routes are allowed.
- Bloodline is studio-first, not artist-first.

Forbidden routes:

- `/artists`
- `/artists/[slug]`
- `/team`
- `/our-artists`

---

## Component Rules

- Build reusable composable components.
- Prefer section-based architecture.
- Use typed props.
- Avoid duplicated layout structures.
- Avoid duplicated business logic.
- Use reusable variants when possible.

---

## SEO Rules

- Metadata must be generated centrally.
- Use schema utilities from `src/lib/schema.ts`.
- Support canonical URLs correctly.
- Avoid duplicate regional SEO content.
- Maintain proper heading hierarchy.

---

## TypeScript Rules

- Use strict typing.
- Do not use `any`.
- Validate external data with Zod.
- Share reusable interfaces from `src/types`.

---

## Performance Rules

- Use `next/image`.
- Avoid oversized media payloads.
- Avoid excessive client-side JavaScript.
- Avoid unnecessary dependencies.
- Prioritize fast LCP and low hydration cost.

---

## Forbidden Patterns

Never introduce:

- Pages Router
- hardcoded region copy
- artist profile systems
- duplicated metadata logic
- duplicated route logic
- uncontrolled client rendering
- fake testimonial systems
- random arbitrary architecture
- direct Airtable calls inside components
- Contentlayer

---

## Scalability Rules

- Future regions must plug into existing config architecture.
- Do not create region-specific forks of the application.
- Keep architecture reusable and centralized.

---

## Final Principle

Prioritize:

- server-first architecture
- config-driven systems
- reusable composition
- SEO safety
- performance
- scalability
- architectural consistency